    "question_text": "Two parallel lines AB and CD are intersected by a transversal at\npoints O (on AB) and C (on CD). The transversal extends beyond O\nto a point P such that C, O, and P are collinear. A point A lies on line\nAB, and segment AP is drawn. It is given that AO = OP and OCD =\n50°. Find the measure of OAP.",
