    "question_text": "To measure the height AB of a pavilion (from top A to ground BD), a step DE\n(DE = BC = 0.6) of the same height as the pavilion step BC is placed beside it.\nGiven that A, B, C are collinear, a mirror is placed at point G on the platform where\nCG = 12.0. If the top A is visible in the mirror at point E where GE = 2.0 and the\nobserver's height EF = 1.6, what is the approximate height of the pavilion AB?",
