    "model": "mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct",
    "run_number": 1,
    "model_output": {
      "ANSWER": "24.1",
      "REASONING": "To find the angle of approach (theta), we can use the trigonometric function tangent, which is defined as the ratio of the opposite side to the adjacent side in a right triangle. In this case, the opposite side is the height of the plane above the ground (10369 metres), and the adjacent side is the horizontal distance from the plane to the runway (23444 metres). The formula for the tangent of an angle is: tan(theta) = opposite / adjacent. Substituting the given values, we get: tan(theta) = 10369 / 23444. To find theta, we take the arctangent (inverse tangent) of both sides: theta = arctan(10369 / 23444). Using a calculator, we find: theta ≈ 24.1 degrees."
    },
    "status": "OK"
